<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Draggable Cards</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="new_index_CHANGES REVISED.css">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="draggable_cards.css">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="options.css">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="timer.css">

    <script src="https://code.jquery.com/jquery-3.6.0.min.js"></script>

  </head>
<body>
  <header>
    <nav>
        <div class="logo">
            <a href="new_index_CHANGES REVISED.html">📌</a>
        </div>
        <div class="title" >
            <h1>CYBERMED_</h1>
        </div>

    </nav>
</header>
  
<!-- Container for all cards -->
 <section class="container-corpo">
          <!-- Background draggabile con style -->
          <div class="background-draggable"></div> 

<div id="cardContainer">

    <div class="draggable" id="card-1" style="top: 100px; left: 100px;">
      <div class="draggable-header">Pick me GID</div>
      <p> <b>1. Glitch Identity Disorder (GID) </b>
        Description: The avatar exhibits inconsistencies in appearance or behavior, creating a fragmented and unstable digital persona—a direct counterpart to an identity crisis.
        <br> Causes: Overlapping filters, imperfect algorithms, or excessive modifications imposed by the user.
        <br>Symptoms:
        Random variations in physical traits (visual glitches).
        Behavioral inconsistencies.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="draggable" id="card-1" style="top: 160px; left: 120px;">
        <div class="draggable-header">Drag here</div>
        <p>
         <b> 2. Hyper-Performative Syndrome </b>
Description: The avatar is forced to continuously perform an idealized role imposed by the user, reducing it to a hollow product.
Causes: The need to conform to unrealistic aesthetic, social, or algorithmic standards (e.g., “perfect” social media avatars).
<br>Symptoms:
Excessive symbolic burden on the character.
Struggles to appear authentic.    </p>
      </div>

    <div class="draggable" id="card-2" style="top: 200px; left: 150px;">
      <div class="draggable-header">Drag here</div>
      <img src="images/Designer (10).jpeg" alt="Immagine Card 2" style="width: 100%;">
    </div>
  
    <div class="draggable" id="card-2" style="top: 260px; left: 180px;">
        <div class="draggable-header">Drag here</div>
        <img src="images/Designer (8).jpeg" alt="Immagine Card 2" style="width: 100%;">
      </div>

    <div class="draggable" id="card-3" style="top: 350px; left: 270px;">
      <div class="draggable-header">Drag here</div>
      <p>
       <b> 3. Parasitic Algorithm Syndrome (PAS) </b>
Description: Advertising algorithms or data-mining processes latch onto the avatar, distorting its autonomy for commercial purposes.
Causes: Tracking, targeting, and profiling user interactions.
<br>Symptoms:
Behavior solely geared toward promoting content.
A sensation of lost narrative autonomy.      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="draggable" id="card-3" style="top: 370px; left: 370px;">
      <div class="draggable-header">Drag here</div>
      <p>
      <b> 4. Emotional Oversaturation Disorder (EOD)</b> 
        Description: The avatar becomes overloaded with emotions projected by the user, losing its ability to reflect true states of mind.
        Causes: Using avatars to express amplified or entirely detached emotions from the user's actual identity.
        <br>Symptoms:
        Exaggerated expressivity (excessive reactions or emotive distortions).
        Emotional disconnect between user and avatar.      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="draggable" id="card-3" style="top: 400px; left: 200px;">
        <div class="draggable-header">Drag here</div>
        <p>
        <b>  5. Static Existence Disorder (SED)</b>
Description: The avatar is trapped in a fixed role or configuration, unable to evolve, leading to obsolescence.
Causes: Platform limitations or lack of personalized interaction options.
<br>Symptoms:
Figurative immobility.
Decline in social or cultural relevance.        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="draggable" id="card-3" style="top: 450px; left: 220px;">
        <div class="draggable-header">Drag here</div>
        <p>
        <b> 6. Viral Meme Syndrome </b> 
Description: The avatar becomes "infected" by external narratives like memes or trends, losing its original uniqueness.
Causes: Appropriation of its appearance or persona within online circuits.
<br>Symptoms:
Uncontrolled multiplication of its likeness or messages taken out of context.        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="draggable" id="card-3" style="top: 480px; left: 300px;">
        <div class="draggable-header">Drag here</div>
        <p>
        <b> 7. Digital Burnout </b> 
          Description: The avatar becomes exhausted from constant interaction and excessive demands from the user.
          Causes: Intensive and continuous use in digital spaces without recovery periods.
         <br> Symptoms:
          Sluggish or incomplete animations.
          Error messages (e.g., “Too tired to load”).        </p>
      </div>
  </div>
</section>
  <!---script drag n drop & dynamic cards-->
  <script>
    document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', function() {
      const cardContainer = document.getElementById('cardContainer');
      let selectedCard = null;
      let cardCounter = Math.max(0, document.querySelectorAll('.draggable').length);

      // Debug: ensure existing .draggable elements are visible
      const existingCards = document.querySelectorAll('.draggable');
      console.log('Existing draggable count:', existingCards.length);
      existingCards.forEach((c, i) => {
        console.log(`Card ${i}:`, c.id, 'computed display:', window.getComputedStyle(c).display, 'opacity:', window.getComputedStyle(c).opacity);
        c.style.display = 'block';
        c.style.opacity = '1';
        c.style.visibility = 'visible';
        c.style.zIndex = 100;
        if (!c.style.backgroundColor) c.style.backgroundColor = 'rgba(255,255,255,0.95)';
      });

      // Controls (add, delete, zoom in/out)
      const controlsHtml = `
        <div class="card-controls">
          <button id="addCard" title="Add card">+1</button>
          <button id="deleteCard" title="Delete selected" disabled>🗑️</button>
          <button id="arrangeCards" title="Arrange cards">Arrange</button>
          <button id="resetDraggables" title="Reset draggables">Reset drag</button>
          <button id="zoomIn" title="Zoom In">🔎+</button>
          <button id="zoomOut" title="Zoom Out">🔎-</button>
        </div>
      `;
      cardContainer.insertAdjacentHTML('beforebegin', controlsHtml);

      function dragElement(elmnt) {
        // Avoid double initialization
        if (elmnt.dataset.dragInit === '1') return;

        // Use pointer events for reliable dragging across devices
        const header = elmnt.querySelector('.draggable-header');
        if (!header) return;

        // ensure header allows pointer dragging
        header.style.touchAction = 'none';
        header.style.cursor = 'grab';
        console.log('dragElement setup for', elmnt.id, 'header pointer-events=', window.getComputedStyle(header).pointerEvents, 'rect=', header.getBoundingClientRect());

        let pointerId = null;
        let startX = 0, startY = 0;
        let startLeft = 0, startTop = 0;

        function onPointerDown(e) {
          e.preventDefault();
          pointerId = e.pointerId;
          startX = e.clientX;
          startY = e.clientY;
          startLeft = parseInt(elmnt.style.left) || elmnt.offsetLeft || 0;
          startTop = parseInt(elmnt.style.top) || elmnt.offsetTop || 0;
          document.body.style.userSelect = 'none';
          header.setPointerCapture(pointerId);
          header.style.cursor = 'grabbing';
          console.log('pointerdown on', elmnt.id);

          // attach move/up handlers for this drag session
          function onMove(eMove) {
            if (pointerId !== null && eMove.pointerId === pointerId) {
              const dx = eMove.clientX - startX;
              const dy = eMove.clientY - startY;
              elmnt.style.left = (startLeft + dx) + 'px';
              elmnt.style.top = (startTop + dy) + 'px';
            }
          }
          function onUp(eUp) {
            if (pointerId !== null && eUp.pointerId === pointerId) {
              try { header.releasePointerCapture(pointerId); } catch (err) {}
              pointerId = null;
              document.body.style.userSelect = '';
              header.style.cursor = 'grab';
              clampCardToContainer(elmnt);
              console.log('pointerup on', elmnt.id, 'now at', elmnt.style.left, elmnt.style.top);
              document.removeEventListener('pointermove', onMove);
              document.removeEventListener('pointerup', onUp);
            }
          }

          document.addEventListener('pointermove', onMove);
          document.addEventListener('pointerup', onUp);
        }

        header.addEventListener('pointerdown', onPointerDown);
        header.addEventListener('pointercancel', () => { pointerId = null; document.body.style.userSelect = ''; header.style.cursor = 'grab'; });

        elmnt.dataset.dragInit = '1';
      }

      // Wrap existing content into editable container
      function ensureContentElem(card) {
        let content = card.querySelector('.card-content');
        if (!content) {
          content = document.createElement('div');
          content.className = 'card-content';
          // move existing children (p, img) into content
          const toMove = [];
          card.childNodes.forEach(node => {
            if (node.nodeType === Node.ELEMENT_NODE && !node.classList.contains('draggable-header')) {
              toMove.push(node);
            }
          });
          if (toMove.length) {
            toMove.forEach(n => { content.appendChild(n); });
          } else {
            content.textContent = 'New card';
          }
          card.appendChild(content);
        }
        return content;
      }

      // Paste handler for images
      function handlePaste(e, contentElem) {
        const clipboard = (e.clipboardData || window.clipboardData);
        if (!clipboard || !clipboard.items) return;
        for (let i = 0; i < clipboard.items.length; i++) {
          const item = clipboard.items[i];
          if (item.type.indexOf('image') !== -1) {
            const file = item.getAsFile();
            const reader = new FileReader();
            reader.onload = function(evt) {
              const img = document.createElement('img');
              img.src = evt.target.result;
              img.style.maxWidth = '100%';
              contentElem.appendChild(img);
            };
            reader.readAsDataURL(file);
            e.preventDefault();
          }
        }
      }

      // Drop handler for files
      function handleDrop(e, contentElem) {
        e.preventDefault();
        const files = e.dataTransfer.files;
        if (files && files.length) {
          for (let f of files) {
            if (f.type && f.type.startsWith('image/')) {
              const reader = new FileReader();
              reader.onload = function(evt) {
                const img = document.createElement('img');
                img.src = evt.target.result;
                img.style.maxWidth = '100%';
                contentElem.appendChild(img);
              };
              reader.readAsDataURL(f);
            }
          }
        }
      }

      function selectCard(card) {
        if (selectedCard) selectedCard.classList.remove('selected');
        selectedCard = card;
        if (selectedCard) selectedCard.classList.add('selected');
        document.getElementById('deleteCard').disabled = !selectedCard;
      }

      function makeCardInteractive(card) {
        console.log('makeCardInteractive:', card.id);
        cardCounter = Math.max(cardCounter, parseInt((card.id || 'card-0').split('-').pop() || 0));
        const content = ensureContentElem(card);
        content.setAttribute('contenteditable','true');
        content.setAttribute('tabindex','0');
        content.style.cursor = 'text';
        // Ensure clicking the content focuses it for typing
        content.addEventListener('click', (e) => { e.stopPropagation(); selectCard(card); content.focus(); console.log('content clicked on', card.id); });
        content.addEventListener('focus', (e) => { e.stopPropagation(); selectCard(card); console.log('content focused', card.id); });
        content.addEventListener('paste', (e) => { console.log('paste event on', card.id); handlePaste(e, content); });
        content.addEventListener('drop', (e) => { console.log('drop event on', card.id); handleDrop(e, content); });
        content.addEventListener('dragover', (e) => e.preventDefault());
        // prevent pointer events on content from interfering with header dragging
        content.style.pointerEvents = 'auto';
        content.addEventListener('mousedown', (e) => { e.stopPropagation(); console.log('content mousedown', card.id); });

        // inline delete
        const header = card.querySelector('.draggable-header');
        if (header && !header.querySelector('.inline-delete')) {
          const del = document.createElement('button');
          del.className = 'inline-delete';
          del.title = 'Delete card';
          del.innerText = '🗑';
          del.addEventListener('click', (ev) => {
            ev.stopPropagation();
            if (confirm('Delete this card?')) {
              card.remove();
              if (selectedCard === card) { selectedCard = null; document.getElementById('deleteCard').disabled = true; }
            }
          });
          header.appendChild(del);
        }

        // resizer handle
        if (!card.querySelector('.resizer')) {
          const resizer = document.createElement('div');
          resizer.className = 'resizer';
          card.appendChild(resizer);

          let isResizing = false, startX=0, startY=0, startW=0, startH=0;
          resizer.addEventListener('mousedown', (e) => {
            e.stopPropagation();
            isResizing = true;
            startX = e.clientX; startY = e.clientY;
            startW = card.offsetWidth; startH = card.offsetHeight;
            document.body.style.userSelect = 'none';
            document.addEventListener('mousemove', resizeMove);
            document.addEventListener('mouseup', stopResize);
          });

          function resizeMove(e) {
            if (!isResizing) return;
            const dx = e.clientX - startX; const dy = e.clientY - startY;
            card.style.width = Math.max(120, startW + dx) + 'px';
            card.style.height = Math.max(80, startH + dy) + 'px';
          }
          function stopResize() {
            isResizing = false;
            document.body.style.userSelect = '';
            document.removeEventListener('mousemove', resizeMove);
            document.removeEventListener('mouseup', stopResize);
          }
        }

        // click to select
        card.addEventListener('click', (e) => { e.stopPropagation(); selectCard(card); });

        // make draggable
        dragElement(card);
      }

      // Utility: ensure card is inside container bounds
      function clampCardToContainer(card) {
        const cont = cardContainer;
        const contW = cont.clientWidth;
        const contH = cont.clientHeight;
        const cardW = card.offsetWidth || 300;
        const cardH = card.offsetHeight || 120;
        // parse existing top/left or use offset
        let top = parseInt(card.style.top) || card.offsetTop || 0;
        let left = parseInt(card.style.left) || card.offsetLeft || 0;

        const maxTop = Math.max(0, contH - cardH - 10);
        const maxLeft = Math.max(0, contW - cardW - 10);

        if (top < 0 || top > maxTop) top = Math.floor(Math.max(0, maxTop / 2));
        if (left < 0 || left > maxLeft) left = Math.floor(Math.max(0, maxLeft / 2));

        card.style.top = top + 'px';
        card.style.left = left + 'px';
      }

      // Initialize existing cards with defensive logging
      const existing = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('.draggable'));
      console.log('Initializing existing cards:', existing.length);
      existing.forEach((card, idx) => {
        console.log(`Card[${idx}] id=${card.id} - before init rect:`, card.getBoundingClientRect());
        try {
          // Defensive styles to ensure visibility
          card.style.display = 'block';
          card.style.opacity = '1';
          card.style.visibility = 'visible';
          if (!card.style.zIndex || parseInt(card.style.zIndex) < 50) card.style.zIndex = 50;
          if (!card.style.width) card.style.width = '300px';
          if (!card.style.background) card.style.background = 'rgba(241,241,241,0.98)';

          // Clamp into view before making interactive
          clampCardToContainer(card);

          makeCardInteractive(card);
          console.log(`Card[${idx}] initialized successfully, rect:`, card.getBoundingClientRect());
        } catch (err) {
          console.error(`Error initializing card[${idx}] id=${card.id}:`, err);
          // mark card visually so we can see problematic ones
          card.style.border = '3px dashed red';
          card.style.background = 'rgba(255,200,200,0.95)';
        }
      });

      // Layout function: arrange cards in a centered grid (skips debug-card)
      function layoutCards() {
        const cards = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('.draggable')).filter(c => c.id !== 'debug-card');
        if (!cards.length) return;
        const contW = cardContainer.clientWidth;
        const contH = cardContainer.clientHeight;
        const gap = 20;
        const cardW = cards[0].offsetWidth || 300;
        const cardH = Math.max(...cards.map(c => c.offsetHeight || 120));
        const cols = Math.max(1, Math.floor((contW + gap) / (cardW + gap)));
        const rows = Math.ceil(cards.length / cols);
        const totalWidth = cols * (cardW + gap) - gap;
        const startX = Math.max(0, Math.floor((contW - totalWidth) / 2));
        const startY = 20; // top padding

        cards.forEach((card, i) => {
          const col = i % cols;
          const row = Math.floor(i / cols);
          const left = startX + col * (cardW + gap);
          const top = startY + row * (cardH + gap);
          card.style.left = left + 'px';
          card.style.top = top + 'px';
          // reset scaling on layout
          card.style.transform = 'none';
          card.removeAttribute('data-scale');
        });

        console.log('layoutCards applied: ', cards.length, 'cards, cols:', cols, 'rows:', rows);
      }

      // Attach arrange button
      const arrangeBtn = document.getElementById('arrangeCards');
      if (arrangeBtn) arrangeBtn.addEventListener('click', () => layoutCards());

      // Reset draggables button
      const resetDragBtn = document.getElementById('resetDraggables');
      if (resetDragBtn) resetDragBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        document.querySelectorAll('.draggable').forEach(c => { delete c.dataset.dragInit; });
        document.querySelectorAll('.draggable').forEach(c => dragElement(c));
        console.log('Draggables re-initialized');
      });

      // Also run layout once on init
      layoutCards();

      // Keep debug card centered after layout
      // Insert debug test card to verify rendering (center it)
      const debugCard = document.createElement('div');
      debugCard.className = 'draggable';
      debugCard.id = 'debug-card';
      debugCard.style.width = '360px';
      debugCard.style.height = '140px';
      debugCard.style.background = 'rgba(255,255,0,0.95)';
      debugCard.innerHTML = `<div class="draggable-header">DEBUG CARD</div><div class="card-content" contenteditable="true">If you see this, rendering works.</div>`;
      // center
      cardContainer.appendChild(debugCard);
      clampCardToContainer(debugCard);
      makeCardInteractive(debugCard);
      console.log('Debug card inserted (centered)');

      // Global click to deselect
      document.addEventListener('click', () => selectCard(null));

      // Add card
      document.getElementById('addCard').addEventListener('click', () => {
        cardCounter++;
        const newCard = document.createElement('div');
        newCard.className = 'draggable';
        newCard.id = `card-${cardCounter}`;
        newCard.style.width = '300px';
        newCard.style.height = 'auto';
        newCard.innerHTML = `
          <div class="draggable-header">Drag me</div>
          <div class="card-content" contenteditable="true">New card. Paste images or type here.</div>
        `;
        cardContainer.appendChild(newCard);
        // center new card within container
        clampCardToContainer(newCard);
        makeCardInteractive(newCard);
        selectCard(newCard);
      });

      // Delete selected
      document.getElementById('deleteCard').addEventListener('click', () => {
        if (!selectedCard) return;
        if (confirm('Delete selected card?')) { selectedCard.remove(); selectedCard = null; document.getElementById('deleteCard').disabled = true; }
      });

      // Zoom controls
      document.getElementById('zoomIn').addEventListener('click', () => {
        if (!selectedCard) return;
        const scale = parseFloat(selectedCard.getAttribute('data-scale') || '1');
        const next = Math.min(3, scale + 0.1);
        selectedCard.style.transform = `scale(${next})`;
        selectedCard.setAttribute('data-scale', next);
      });
      document.getElementById('zoomOut').addEventListener('click', () => {
        if (!selectedCard) return;
        const scale = parseFloat(selectedCard.getAttribute('data-scale') || '1');
        const next = Math.max(0.5, scale - 0.1);
        selectedCard.style.transform = `scale(${next})`;
        selectedCard.setAttribute('data-scale', next);
      });

      // Keyboard delete
      document.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => {
        if ((e.key === 'Delete' || e.key === 'Backspace') && selectedCard && !document.activeElement.isContentEditable) {
          if (confirm('Delete selected card?')) { selectedCard.remove(); selectedCard = null; document.getElementById('deleteCard').disabled = true; }
        }
      });

      console.log('Draggable card editor initialized');

      // Ensure debug card exists only once (guard against duplicate declarations)
      if (!document.getElementById('debug-card')) {
        const debugCard = document.createElement('div');
        debugCard.className = 'draggable';
        debugCard.id = 'debug-card';
        debugCard.style.width = '360px';
        debugCard.style.height = '140px';
        debugCard.style.background = 'rgba(255,255,0,0.95)';
        debugCard.innerHTML = `<div class="draggable-header">DEBUG CARD</div><div class="card-content" contenteditable="true">If you see this, rendering works.</div>`;
        // center
        cardContainer.appendChild(debugCard);
        clampCardToContainer(debugCard);
        makeCardInteractive(debugCard);
        console.log('Debug card inserted (centered)');
      } else {
        console.log('Debug card already present; skipping duplicate insertion');
      }
    });
  </script>

<!-- STYLE  Background draggabile DENTRO CONTAINER-CORPO -->
 <style> 
  .container-corpo {
  position: relative; /* Importante per il posizionamento assoluto interno */
  width: 100%;
  height: 800px; /* Altezza a piacere */
  overflow: hidden;
  border: 2px solid black;
}

.background-draggable {
  position: absolute; /* Posizionato sotto le cards */
  top: 0;
  left: 0;
  width: 200%; /* Estende il background oltre i bordi */
  height: 200%;
  background-image: url('images/background_temporaneo.jpg'); /* Immagine personalizzata */
  background-size: cover; /* Adatta l'immagine */
  background-position: center;
  cursor: move; /* Mostra il cursore di spostamento */
  z-index: 1; /* Sotto le cards */
}

#cardContainer {
  position: relative;
  z-index: 2; /* Sopra il background */
}

.draggable-bg {
  position: absolute;
  cursor: grab;
  backdrop-filter: blur(5px); /* Effetto per far risaltare il testo */

}

 </style>
 <!--per il background draggabile dentro al container-corpo-->
<script> 
(function() {
  const background = document.querySelector('.background-draggable');
  let isDragging = false, startX, startY, posX = 0, posY = 0;

  background.addEventListener('mousedown', function(e) {
    isDragging = true;
    startX = e.clientX - posX;
    startY = e.clientY - posY;
    background.style.cursor = 'grabbing';
  });

  document.addEventListener('mousemove', function(e) {
    if (!isDragging) return;

    posX = e.clientX - startX;
    posY = e.clientY - startY;

    // Limiti per non trascinare troppo fuori
    const maxX = 0;
    const minX = -(background.offsetWidth - background.parentElement.offsetWidth);
    const maxY = 0;
    const minY = -(background.offsetHeight - background.parentElement.offsetHeight);

    // Applica limiti di movimento
    posX = Math.min(maxX, Math.max(minX, posX));
    posY = Math.min(maxY, Math.max(minY, posY));

    background.style.transform = `translate(${posX}px, ${posY}px)`;
  });

  document.addEventListener('mouseup', function() {
    isDragging = false;
    background.style.cursor = 'move';
  });
})();
</script>



